Courier New leaves those annoying gaps in the walls of rooms, but the 
glyphs are "squarer" than Lucida Console.  At 10 pt, Courier New gives 
me a window that's 640x384 (aspect ratio ~1.7), while Lucida Console is 
720x312 (aspect ratio of ~2.3)  By comparison, using Terminal gives me a 
window that's 480x288, which is the same aspect ratio as using Courier 
New but the size is just too darn small.

